# mhvtl raw-disk bay map (Phase 2, Stage A).
#
# Binds a library Import/Export (MAP) slot to a physical disk bay. Inserting a
# formatted raw-disk cartridge into a bay makes it appear in that MAP slot; a
# normal SCSI MOVE MEDIUM then loads it into a drive. The cartridge barcode is
# NOT configured here -- it is discovered from the disk's MVTL superblock.
#
# Format (one bay per line; '#' comments and blank lines are ignored):
#
#   <library_id>  <map_slot>  <by-path-device>  [by-id=<identifier>]
#
#   library_id       mhvtl library instance id (the systemd vtllibrary@<id>)
#   map_slot         1-based MAP / Import-Export slot index within that library.
#                    NOTE (Stage A): recorded as the operator's intended binding,
#                    but the current load path lets the library assign the first
#                    free MAP slot -- a cartridge is not guaranteed to land in
#                    exactly this slot yet. Deterministic slot placement is a
#                    Stage B enhancement (needs a library-protocol extension).
#   by-path-device   stable /dev/disk/by-path/... node for the bay -- THE binding.
#                    Never use /dev/sdX (not stable across reboots/hotplug).
#   by-id=...        optional /dev/disk/by-id/... recorded for audit only;
#                    it is never used to resolve the device.
#
# Examples:
#
# 10  1  /dev/disk/by-path/pci-0000:01:00.0-sas-phy0-lun-0
# 10  2  /dev/disk/by-path/pci-0000:01:00.0-sas-phy1-lun-0  by-id=wwn-0x5000c500aabbccdd
